#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Loans"
msgstr "Pozajmice (krediti)"

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "Understanding Loans"
msgstr "Razumijevanje pozajmica"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section provides an overview of how &kappname; handles loans. Loan "
"regulations and customs vary from locality to locality. For detailed "
"explanations of loans, as well as information on local regulations and "
"customs, please see other resources."
msgstr ""
"Ova sekcija pruža pregled kako &kappname;  radi sa pozajmicama. Reugalcije i "
"običaji pozajmica se razlikuju od mjesta do mjesta. Za detaljnije "
"objašnjenje pozajmica kao i informacija o lokalnim regulacijama i običajima, "
"molimo vas da pogledate druge resurse."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A loan is an agreement under which a borrower receives money from a lender "
"and agrees to repay the money at some future date. &kappname; allows you to "
"track loans by which you, as borrower, borrow money from or, as lender, lend "
"money to someone else. Most individuals borrow more than they lend, so you "
"will generally be the borrower and a finance company will generally be the "
"lender. If you lend money to a family member or a friend, you can use "
"&kappname; to keep track of this loan as well."
msgstr ""
"Pozajmica je dogovor pod kojim neka osoba prima novac od druge osobe i slaže "
"se da će vratiti taj novac u budućnosti. &kappname; vam omogućava da pratite "
"pozajmice kao osoba koja je posudila novac od nekoga ili kao osoba koja je "
"posudila novac nekome drugom. Većina ljudi više posuđuje od drugih nego što "
"posuđuje drugima, pa ćete često biti osoba koja posuđuje a finansijska "
"kompanija će biti izvor novca. Ukoliko posudite novac članu porodice ili "
"prijatelju, možete koristiti &kappname; da pratite i tu pozajmicu."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This guide will assume that you are borrowing from some sort of finance "
"company, but the topics discussed here apply equally well to loans that you "
"might make to a person. The main difference between borrowing and lending "
"money is that an expense category is used to keep track of interest when "
"borrowing money and an income category is used to keep track of interest "
"when lending money."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj vodič će pretpostaviti da posuđujete od neke finansijske kompanije, ali "
"teme o kojima se ovdje diskutuje se odnose jednako na sve pozajmice. Glavna "
"razlika između posuđivanja novca od nekog i nekome je što se u prvom slučaju "
"koristi rashod kategorija a u drugom prihod kategorija prilikom računanja "
"kamata."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Loan Principal"
msgstr "Glavnica pozajmice"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The amount that is lent out is called the <quote>loan amount</quote> or "
"<quote>principal</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Iznos koji se posuđuje se naziva <quote>iznos pozajmice</quote> ili "
"<quote>glavnica</quote>."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Term"
msgstr "Rok"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The period of a loan is called its <quote>term</quote> of the loan. At the "
"end of the term, the entirety of the principal will have been returned to "
"the borrower. Terms are generally expressed in weeks, months, or years. A "
"term can also be expressed by the number of payments. For example, a one "
"year loan with weekly repayments could be described as a one year loan or a "
"loan with 52 repayments."
msgstr ""
"Period pozajmice se naziva <quote>rok</quote> pozajmice. Na kraju roka "
"cjelina glavnice će biti vraćena osobi čiji je novac izvorno bio. Rokovi se "
"uopšteno iskazuju u sedmicam, mjesecima ili godinama. Rok se također može "
"prikazati brojem isplata. Npr., jednogodišnja pozajmica sa sedmičnim "
"otplatama se može opisati kao jednogodišnja pozajmica sa 52 otplate."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Repayments"
msgstr "Otplate"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The repayment of the principal to the lender is generally not done as a lump "
"sum. Instead, a series of repayments are made, each representing a portion "
"of the principal. Such repayments are sometimes known as <quote>amortization "
"payments</quote> and in &kappname; <quote>Amortization</quote> is defined as "
"the act of paying off a loan in installments."
msgstr ""
"Otplata glavnice se uopšteno ne vrši kao ukupna suma. Umjesto toga, serija "
"otplata se vrši, gdje svaka predstavlja dio glavnice. Takve otplate su "
"poznate i kao <quote>amortizacijske otplate</quote> i u &kappname; "
"<quote>Amortizacija</quote> je definisana kao čin otplate pozajmice."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Payment Frequency"
msgstr "Frekvencija otplate"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The frequency of installments is referred to as <quote>Payment Frequency</"
"quote> in &kappname;. Examples of period might be weekly, bi-weekly, "
"monthly, quarterly, or yearly. In the US, periodic payments are most "
"commonly made every month, therefore the loan's period is one month."
msgstr ""
"Frekvencija otplate se odnosi na <quote>Payment Frequency</quote> u "
"&kappname;. Primjeri perioda mogu biti sedmično, svake dvije sedmice, "
"mjesečno, kvartalno ili godišno. U Americi, periodične otplate su najčešće "
"mjesečne, pa je period pozajmica jedan mjesec."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interest Rate"
msgstr "Kamatna stopa"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For the privilege of being able to use the money, the borrower will pay the "
"lender a fee called the <quote>interest</quote>, normally expressed as a "
"percentage of the amount of the principal over a defined period. Interest "
"rates can be fixed, where the interest rate does not change over the "
"lifetime of the loan, or variable, where the interest rate can change over "
"time. Typically, interest payments are included with each periodic repayment."
msgstr ""
"Zbog privilegije da koristi novac, osoba koja pozajmi novac od nekoga mora "
"plaćati i naknadu koja se zove <quote>kamatna stopa</quote>, uobičajeno "
"izraženom u procentima u odnosu na glavnicu preko definisanog perioda. "
"Kamatne stope mogu biti fiksne, gdje se iste ne mijenjaju tokom života "
"pozajmice, ili mogu varirati tokom tog istog perioda. Uobičajeno su otplate "
"kamatne stope uračunate u periodične otplate."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "Periodic Repayments"
msgstr "Periodične otplate"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since these repayments are generally made on some sort of scheduled basis, "
"such as weekly, monthly, quarterly, or yearly, they are referred to as "
"<quote>periodic repayments</quote>. The sum of all periodic repayments plus "
"the final repayment will add up to the loan principal plus the interest."
msgstr ""
"Pošto se ove otplate često vrše po nekom određenom rasporedu, kao što je "
"sedmično, mjesečno, kvartalno ili godišnje, nazivaju se <quote>periodične "
"otplate</quote>. Suma svih periodičnih otplata plus finalna otplata će biti "
"jednake glavnici pozajmice plu kamatnoj stopi."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fees"
msgstr "Nadoknada"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There may be other fees besides interest that are required to be paid with "
"every installment. These are called <quote>recurring fees</quote>. Examples "
"of recurring fees include (but are not necessarily limited to):"
msgstr ""
"Moguće je da će biti drugih naknada osim kamatne stope koje treba platiti "
"pri svakoj otplati. One se nazivaju <quote>ponavljajuće naknade</quote>. "
"Primjeri ponavljajućih naknada uključuju(ali nisu striktno ograničene na):"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<quote>Impound</quote> or <quote>escrow</quote> account payments. (Payments "
"of this sort are commonly used to hold funds to pay annual or bi-annual "
"property taxes.)"
msgstr ""
"<quote>Zaplijena</quote> ili <quote>poveznica</quote> otplate računa. "
"(Otplate ove vrste su uobičajene priliko zadržavanja sredstava radi otplate "
"dvogodišnjih poreza na imovinu."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mortgage insurance"
msgstr "Osiguranje hipoteke"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disability insurance"
msgstr "Osiguranje invalidnosti"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Loan account maintenance fees"
msgstr "Naknade održavanja računa pozajmice"

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "Rezime"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In summary, the borrower receives a lump sum from the lender at the start of "
"the loan. The borrower makes a periodic payment to the lender. The periodic "
"payment is the sum of the principal payment (which is used to pay down the "
"balance of the loan) plus the interest payment (which rewards the lender for "
"allowing the use of the money by the borrower) plus any recurring fees "
"(which cover any incidentals.) At the end of the loan, the borrower has paid "
"back the entire principal."
msgstr ""
"Ukratko, dužnik na početku dobija ukupnu sumu novca pozajmice od zajmodavca. "
"Dužnik vrši periodične otplate zajmodavcu. Periodične otplate na kraju "
"predstavljaju sumu otplate glavnice (koja se koristi da se otplati bilans "
"pozajmice) plus otplate kamatne stope (koje negrađuje zajmodavca što je "
"dozvolio dužniku da koristi novac) plus bilo koje ponavljajuće nadoknade "
"(koje pokrivaju bilo kakve incidente.) Na kraju pozajmice, dužnik je "
"otplatio cijelu glavnicu zajmodavcu."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Primjer"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For an example, you might borrow $25,000.00 for a new auto and agree to pay "
"the bank one payment each month for 60 months. The interest rate on the loan "
"might be 5.5%."
msgstr ""
"Npr. možete posuditi $25,000.00 za novo auto i dogovoriti se da plaćate "
"banci jednu otplatu svaki mjesec tokom 60 mjeseci. Kamatna stopa pozajmice "
"može biti 5.5%."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this scenario, the loan amount is $25,000.00. The term of the loan is 60 "
"months or 5 years. The term of the loan could also be described as 60 "
"payments since there will be one payment per month for 5 years. The "
"repayment frequency is one month since periodic repayments will be made once "
"a month. The periodic repayment, which is calculated by &kappname;, would be "
"$477.53."
msgstr ""
"U ovom slučaju, iznos pozajmice je $25,000.00. . Period pozajmice je 60 "
"mjeseci ili 5 godina. Rok pozajmice se može opisati i kao 60 otplata pošto "
"će se vršiti jedna otplata mjesečno tokom 5 godina. Frekvencija otplate je "
"jedan mjesec pošto će periodične otplate biti vršene jednom mjesečno. "
"Periodična otplata, koju računa &kappname;, bi bila $477.53."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <quote>loan schedule</quote> is a chart or table that shows the date that "
"a repayment should be made and the amount of each periodic repayment. Often, "
"these schedules break the periodic payment down into its constituent parts: "
"the principal repayment, the interest payment, and the recurring fees "
"payment."
msgstr ""
"<quote>Raspored pozajmice</quote> je tabela koja pokazuje datume kada se "
"otplata treba izvršiti i iznose svake periodične otplate. Često ovi "
"rasporedi dijele periodične isplate u svoje dijelove: otplatu glavnice, "
"kamatnu stopu i otplatu ponavljajuće nadoknade."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a New Loan"
msgstr "Kreiranje nove pozajmice"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kappname;, a loan is a type of account. Therefore, to create a new loan, "
"you begin by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Account</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New Account</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Continue by "
"answering the questions that the wizard poses to you."
msgstr ""
"U &kappname;, pozajmica je tip računa. Zato, da biste kreirali novu "
"pozajmicu, počinjete odabirom <menuchoice><guimenu>Account</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New Account</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Nastavite "
"odgovaranjem na pitanja koja vam čarobnjak postavi."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Optionally, a loan can be associated with a particular institution. If you "
"are borrowing from a mortgage company or a car loan company, you could "
"create an institution entry that describes this firm and associate the "
"institution with your loan. If you are borrowing from your Uncle Ted, there "
"is no requirement to set up an institution."
msgstr ""
"Opcionalno, pozajmica može biti povezana sa određenom institucijom. Ukoliko "
"posuđujete novac od kompanije za hipoteke ili kompanije za pozajmice zbog "
"auta, napravili biste unos za instituciju koji opisuje firmu i povezuje "
"institucije sa vašom pzajmicom. Ukoliko pozajmljujete od ujaka Teda, nije "
"potrebno praviti instituciju."

#. Tag: title
#: details-loans.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Making Extra Principle Repayments On Loans"
msgstr "Vršenje dodatnih otplata kamatnih stopa nad pozajmicom"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you would like to make an extra principal repayment, you can do so. "
"Simply <link linkend=\"details.ledger.transactions\">enter a transaction</"
"link> using the ledger. This extra repayment of principal will be taken into "
"account for the interest calculation that happens for the next periodic "
"payment."
msgstr ""
"Ukoliko želite da izvršite dodatne otplate kamatnih stopa, možete to "
"uraditi. Jednostavno <link linkend=\"details.ledger.transactions\">unesite "
"transakciju </link> upotrebom glavnog pregleda. Ove dodatne otplate kamatne "
"stope će biti uračunate u kalkulaciju za sljedeću kamatnu stopu u sljedećoj "
"periodičnoj otplati."

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Examples of extra principal payments include (but are not necessarily "
"limited to):"
msgstr "Primjeri dodatnih otplata kamatne stope(ali nisu nužno ograničeni na):"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contributing an extra $50 a month"
msgstr "Doprinos dodatnih $50 mjesečno"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Doubling the periodic principal repayment for every period. (The principal "
"repayment can be found for any particular period by referring to the loan "
"schedule.)"
msgstr ""
"Dupliranje kamatne stope periodične otplate za svaki period. (Otplata "
"kamatne stope se može naći za određeni period u rasporedu pozajmica.)"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Making a 13th principal repayment every year. (This assumes a loan that is "
"repaid in monthly installments.)"
msgstr ""
"Izvršenje trinaeste otplate svake godine. (Ovo pretpostavlja da se pozajmica "
"otplaćuje mjesečno.)"

#. Tag: para
#: details-loans.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note: If you are doubling the principal repaid with every periodic payment, "
"you will need to recalculate the loan schedule for each installment. This "
"will allow there to be an accurate value for the required principal "
"repayment with each installment."
msgstr ""
"Bilješka: Ukoliko duplirate glavnicu vraćenu sa svakom periodičnom otplatom, "
"moraćete ponovo izračunati raspored pozajmice za svaku ratu. Ovo će "
"omogučiti da tu bude tačna vrijednost za traženu glavnicu otplate sa svakom "
"ratom."

